tered at the origin. It crosses the negative $y$-axis at the point where $r=4$ and $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959689/assets/0861ee15a875e00738a237d2788e26432c1c4c128ad7510a881f31aebaaff491.png)\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection in polar coordinates is $(4,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47358248-2067-590e-80e1-5d20796434c5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Polar Equation of a Circle Given a Point on the Circumference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5e59746-10ca-52fa-bedc-e6dd385510f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267821} {:answer/id #uuid "7385acb0-f3ba-5d68-a480-390e14febbd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267822} {:answer/id #uuid "7db48f17-4181-5db4-9a78-e670813a17dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267823} {:answer/id #uuid "f1419eb7-de59-5dfb-868e-a68efe4081c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267824} {:answer/id #uuid "cb28811e-3159-5ac6-92a5-c877b1f09320" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1419eb7-de59-5dfb-868e-a68efe4081c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267824} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fe5ed7e-81d1-563c-9305-51d1a9299768" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267820}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "efe7ac63-e273-580d-b8ab-3253ede92761" :question/math-academy-id "q-120186" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959689/assets/f8b8c044d79ce592089365b3918dfae0afc52ef86a71c899abe823c828ab23b0.png)\n\nFind the polar equation of the circle centered at the origin that passes through the point $A(1,-1)$, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "A circle of radius $k$ centered at the origin has the polar equation $r=k.$\n\nWe can compute the radius $k$ of our circle using the Pythagorean theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the circle is $r=\\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47358248-2067-590e-80e1-5d20796434c5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Polar Equation of a Circle Given a Point on the Circumference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1e00824-76b0-59ee-8b69-0e97a3a639e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = 50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089707} {:answer/id #uuid "c77a1706-1358-53d3-a0e8-88be37ed1191" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089708} {:answer/id #uuid "ce8559b8-e522-5427-a7eb-f9a80dfbaaf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = 52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089709} {:answer/id #uuid "eace999b-39fa-5805-96fd-5cf5b43cc102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = 5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089710} {:answer/id #uuid "48f2296b-2101-5f04-ab6e-520c93f3fc31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = \\sqrt{52}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48f2296b-2101-5f04-ab6e-520c93f3fc31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = \\sqrt{52}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089711} :answer-field/id #uuid "faa491b1-521e-5b48-9851-0bd2822e6e20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186089706}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "125edd16-dfa8-5ed1-af01-368de5476e99" :question/math-academy-id "q-17150" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/937/Source/Images/q-17150.png)\n\nFind the polar equation of the circle centered at the origin that passes through the point $A(6, 4)$, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "A circle of radius $k$ centered at the origin has the polar equation $r=k.$\n\nWe can compute the radius $k$ of our circle using the Pythagorean theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{52}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the circle is $r=\\sqrt{52}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93f33baf-c3b5-549a-8eb7-1ab370e9c62b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection of a Polar Circle With an Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be2bfc0a-129c-55c7-acbc-b2cc110aa24f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267828} {:answer/id #uuid "907970b2-a788-51a7-b4a6-174ca7c30e35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be2bfc0a-129c-55c7-acbc-b2cc110aa24f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267828} :answer-field/id #uuid "94e5c21a-548b-5aeb-9cfe-728e1078f31c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267827} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc0429eb-3953-5099-bba2-24f94f7521aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc0429eb-3953-5099-bba2-24f94f7521aa" :answer/type {:db/ident