press the polar angle in radians.\n\nThe point of intersection in polar coordinates is $(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" :question/worked-solution "The polar curve $r=\\frac{23}{6}$ is a circle of radius $\\frac{23}{6}$ centered at the origin. It crosses the positive $y$-axis where $r=\\frac{23}{6}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959689/assets/6cab0604a3a8a45de244519cd407d310e8add3978e13cd20e1ef6b3d38e191fd.png)\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection in polar coordinates is $(\\,\\frac{23}{6},\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47358248-2067-590e-80e1-5d20796434c5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Polar Equation of a Circle Given a Point on the Circumference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbb97adf-370b-5e93-affc-f5bc622e97e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{145}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbb97adf-370b-5e93-affc-f5bc622e97e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{145}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267842} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4156151-2c4b-5001-85f3-5ff8869074e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267841}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb94df5a-9e0f-535f-8cba-1fc2bb995c30" :question/math-academy-id "q-325175" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959689/assets/82744601b054c3aba5f3d117291ccd52e3823db75d158532cbac89c31a99ff27.png)\n\nThe polar equation of the circle centered at the origin that passes through the point $A(8,9)$, as shown above, is$\\,\\,r=$ \n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "A circle of radius $k$ centered at the origin has the polar equation $r=k.$\n\nWe can compute the radius $k$ of our circle using the Pythagorean theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{9}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+81} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{145}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the circle is $r=\\sqrt{145}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "47358248-2067-590e-80e1-5d20796434c5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Polar Equation of a Circle Given a Point on the Circumference"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5b2cae2-321f-58dc-83ab-08b1cea647c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5b2cae2-321f-58dc-83ab-08b1cea647c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267845} :answer-field/id #uuid "203a5109-baee-5991-bc8c-4149c669b848" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267844}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a020aa52-a41b-59b4-a523-caef6a0f3163" :question/math-academy-id "q-325178" :question/problem "The polar equation of the circle that is centered at the origin and that passes through the point $A(1,7)$ is$\\,\\,r=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "A circle of radius $k$ centered at the origin has the polar equation $r=k.$\n\nWe can compute the radius $k$ of our circle using the Pythagorean theorem, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+49} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{50} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the circle is $r=5\\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4034e61-63dc-5f72-8275-e9c81290767d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Gr